<title>USA: U.S. ag attache sees lower India 97/98 cotton crop.</title>
<headline>U.S. ag attache sees lower India 97/98 cotton crop.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>An agricultural attache posted at the U.S. embassy in New Dehli said lower cotton prices are expected to result in a six percent decline in India 1997/98 cotton area and a 1.4 million bale drop in production.</p>
<p>The attache said assuming normal weather conditions, 1997/98 India cotton output is projected at 14.3 million bales.</p>
<p>&quot;While this forecast is below production estimates for the past two years, if realized, it will be one of the largest cotton crops on record,&quot; the attache wrote in a report dated Jan. 15 that was released in Washington.</p>
<p>Attache reports are not official USDA data.</p>
</text>
